{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"location based mesh component selection location based mesh component selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","fileName":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"location based mesh component selection location based mesh component selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","fileName":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection","heading":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Location-based selection identifies vertices, edges, or faces by testing their coordinates against a bounding region. Unlike hardcoded indices, the criterion describes where the desired geometry is, making it more resilient to topology ordering and more suitable for parameterized models.\n\nThe test must define global or local space and decide how compound components qualify. A vertex can be tested directly; an edge or face may require all, any, or a representative point of its vertices to fall within the bounds. Additive selection lets several regions be accumulated before a single mesh operation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"location based mesh component selection location based mesh component selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","fileName":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Location-Based Mesh Component Selection","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Procedural Mesh Editing with bmesh","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}